3. Modifications (AGPL-3.0 section 5(b))

This is a rebranded derivation named POPOPX. The complete change history of
this repository records every modification; the material steps are:

- 2026-11-11, commit e9ca9df6 - 241 paths renamed: source directories and
  Haskell modules (`src/Simplex` to `src/Popopx`), protocol documents, scripts,
  packaging files and the package name (`simplexmq` to `popopxmq`).
- 2026-11-11, commit d1ae1af4 - 412 files, 4071 lines: brand strings replaced
  (simplex -> popopx, Simplex -> Popopx, SimpleX -> POPOPX, SIMPLEX -> POPOPX),
  excluding GitHub URLs to the upstream organisation, ./LICENSE and the notices
  listed in section 2.
- 2026-11-12 - 23 links into this repository's own renamed documents repaired;
  application identifiers updated (apple-app-site-association appID, assetlinks
  package name, APNs topic and team defaults, Play Store links, App Store
  record ID); the xftp web bundle rebuilt from source; this notice added.
- 2026-11-12, commit - 14 lines, 3 files: the preset SMP, XFTP and notification
  server hostnames reverted to the upstream ones they were changed from, because
  the keys embedded with them were never changed (see section 3).
- 2026-11-12, commit - 19 lines, 6 files: the same revert extended past Haskell
  to the non-Haskell holders of those pairs - xftp-web/web/servers.json (12
  addresses and the `presets` member), xftp-web/vite.config.ts (its one reader),
  the four contact links served by a relay of this distribution, and the rebuilt
  xftp web bundle (6). The previous revision of this notice claimed the bundle
  "is generated from a source tree that is not in this repository": that is
  wrong, servers.json is tracked and hand-editable, so the bundle was rebuilt
  here with `npm run build && npm run build:prod`. The rebuild is otherwise
  reproducible - the new file equals the old one with exactly those 6 hostnames
  substituted, verified byte for byte.
- 2026-11-16 - 15 files besides this notice, source delivery only, no protocol or wire
  change: the
  `xftp-server init` configuration template writes `source_code` uncommented, where it
  shipped commented out and so a default XFTP relay conveyed no source in its handshake;
  `generateSite` renders the link pages as it already rendered the index page, and
  `link.html` and `file.html` gained a footer line giving the source of the running
  commit; the runtime Docker image carries ./LICENSE and ./NOTICE and sets the OCI
  `source` and `licenses` labels; a GitHub release body states the corresponding-source
  offer; the 7 module headers that read `License: AGPL-3` now add that this distribution
  conveys the work under AGPL-3.0-only.
- 2026-11-16, same day - 4 files besides this notice, source completeness: `xftp-web/.gitignore` no longer
  ignores `package-lock.json`, which is now tracked, so the shipped xftp web bundle can
  be resolved to the dependency versions that built it; the Apache-2.0 license texts of
  the two vendored C trees were taken from the pinned commit of each submodule and are
  distributed as `cbits/LICENSE-blst` and `cbits/LICENSE-libbbs`, added to
  `extra-source-files` so a source distribution conveys them together with the sources
  they cover (see section 2).
- 2026-11-16, same day - README.md carried the SHA-256 of `install.sh` as that script
  stood at the snapshot commit (`53fcdb4c…`), but the branding change and the later
  removal of cloud provisioning both rewrote the script, so anyone following the
  documented one-liner failed its own checksum gate with "SHA-256 checksum is
  incorrect!". The recorded value is now what `install.sh` hashes to at this commit, and
  the build workflow gained a step that recomputes it and fails when README disagrees: a
  checksum quoted in prose is the one end a script change cannot move by itself.

Modifications that change behaviour or interoperability, not just names:

- Service URI scheme is `popopx:` instead of the upstream scheme
  (src/Popopx/Messaging/ServiceScheme.hs).
- Key-derivation label strings were changed to `POPOPX*` - `POPOPXSbChainInit`,
  `POPOPXSbChain`, `POPOPXX3DH`, `POPOPXVerifyCode`, `POPOPXRootRatchet`,
  `POPOPXChainRatchet`, `POPOPXContactLink`, `POPOPXInvLink`, `POPOPXService` -
  and the BBS badge header to `POPOPX badges v1`. These derivations do NOT
  interoperate with upstream servers or agents, and data produced under the
  upstream labels cannot be decrypted by this version, or the reverse.
- Prometheus metric names are `popopx_smp_*`.
- Preset server hostnames are NOT changed: `smp*.simplex.im`, `xftp*.simplex.im`
  and `ntf*.simplex.im`, together with the public keys and .onion addresses
  embedded with them, in every place those pairs appear. The Haskell half is
  src/Popopx/FileTransfer/Client/Presets.hs,
  src/Popopx/Messaging/Agent/Protocol.hs (`extraSMPServerHosts`) and the
  m20220811 migration; the non-Haskell half of the same values is
  xftp-web/web/servers.json with the `presets` member read by
  xftp-web/vite.config.ts, the build product
  apps/xftp-server/static/xftp-web-bundle/index.js, and the four contact links
  a server of this distribution serves in
  apps/common/Web/static/{index,link}.html and
  apps/xftp-server/static/file.html. In the last three, only the relay host
  inside the address moved back: the `popopx.chat` link domain on the same lines
  is this fork's own (see below).
  This fork does not operate servers, and a hostname paired with a key that is
  not that server's makes the preset unusable rather than neutral: file
  transfers could not verify any XFTP server, and
  `extraSMPServerHosts` plus the m20220811 migration, which are both keyed on
  the host, stopped matching any stored row. The Flux list in servers.json is
  reverted for a related reason: those servers belong to Flux, and taking over
  their hostname routes Flux's service under this fork's name.
  These values move only in the change that installs this fork's own server
  keys.
- Docker image organisation is `popopxchat`; installation paths are
  `/etc/popopx`, `/etc/popopx-xftp` and `/var/lib/popopx`, and the server
  management scripts are `popopx-servers-*`.

Intentionally not changed: the SQLite user-defined function
`simplex_xor_md5_combine` (src/Popopx/Messaging/Agent/Store/SQLite.hs). Its name
is persisted inside existing database triggers, so renaming it would break
databases that were already created.


4. Corresponding source (AGPL-3.0 section 13)

Users who interact remotely with a modified server offered by this work are
provided the complete corresponding source, which is this repository:

  https://github.com/popopx-chat/popopxmq

This includes the build scripts and the sources of generated artifacts that are
distributed with the binaries. The xftp web bundle served by xftp-server
(apps/xftp-server/static/xftp-web-bundle/) is generated, never hand-edited: it is
produced from xftp-web/ with

  npm install && npm run build && npm run build:prod

and the files `index.js`, `crypto.worker.js` and `index.css` from
xftp-web/dist-web/assets/ are copied into the bundle directory.

Where this offer is made from, as of 2026-11-16:

- a server that has `source_code` in its `[INFORMATION]` section sends it in the
  handshake, for SMP and for XFTP, when the negotiated protocol version carries
  server information; both `smp-server init` and `xftp-server init` write that
  field uncommented;
- the static pages a relay serves - `index.html`, `link.html`, `file.html` - print
  the source address together with the commit the binary was built from;
- an image built from ./Dockerfile carries ./LICENSE and ./NOTICE under
  /usr/share/doc/popopxmq/, the Apache-2.0 texts of the C it embeds under
  /usr/share/doc/popopxmq/third-party/, and sets
  `org.opencontainers.image.source` and `org.opencontainers.image.licenses`;
- a GitHub release of this repository states the offer in its body.

Closed the same day, in the same change: the dependency versions behind the shipped
xftp web bundle are now in the repository, because `xftp-web/package-lock.json` is no
longer gitignored; and the license terms of the vendored `cbits/blst` and
`cbits/libbbs` sources travel with the package, as `cbits/LICENSE-blst` and
`cbits/LICENSE-libbbs` (see section 2).

One gap remains, and it is not a file change: `install.sh`, README.md and the
`blob/stable/` links that the served pages and the generated configuration print all
name a `stable` branch. A branch of that name now exists in this repository's history,
but it reaches the outside world only once it is published; until then this offer is
reachable through `master` and the release tags.


